== About This Document

This reference covers the four core REST APIs that power the **{product-name}**: Trip Management, Driver & Vehicle Management, Real-Time Telemetry, and Fare Pricing. Together they orchestrate the complete lifecycle of a taxi dispatch operation — from a passenger booking a ride through to fare settlement, driver shift management, and fleet compliance.

The platform is built on an event-driven microservice architecture. Each API runs as an independent service. Domain events propagate automatically across services as trips move through their lifecycle states — no manual cross-service calls are required from client applications.

[cols="1,2,1,1", options="header"]
|===
| Service | Responsibility | Port | Base Path

| Trip Service
| Trip booking, lifecycle, scheduling
| 10005
| `/api/v1/trips`

| Driver Service
| Driver profiles, shifts, vehicles, ratings, compliance
| 10001
| `/api/v1/drivers`, `/api/v1/shifts`, `/api/v1/vehicles`

| Telemetry Service
| Real-time GPS ingestion and geospatial driver discovery
| 10002
| `/api/v1/locations`

| Pricing Service
| Fare estimation, zone pricing, toll gates, time windows
| 10003
| `/api/v1/pricing`
|===

