== Driver & Vehicle Management API

*Base URL:* `http://localhost:10001`

The Driver & Vehicle API is the authoritative registry for every human and machine that operates on the Tanzim network. It is a multi-domain service — rather than a single narrow responsibility, it owns the full scope of fleet governance: who is allowed to drive, which vehicle they operate, when they are working, how passengers have rated them, and whether their conduct meets the platform's safety and compliance standards.

This service is designed to serve three distinct consumer groups simultaneously. **Driver apps** use it for authentication, shift management, location updates, and viewing their own performance data. **Passenger apps** use it indirectly — the dispatch engine queries driver availability and proximity data here before assigning a trip. **Fleet operators and compliance teams** use the administrative endpoints for driver onboarding, licence monitoring, suspension management, and regulatory reporting.

The service integrates with Keycloak for identity management. Every driver registration provisions a Keycloak account, and all driver-facing JWT tokens are issued and validated through that identity provider. The Driver Service holds the Tanzim-specific profile data (operator assignment, licence details, vehicle assignment, behavioral scores) while Keycloak holds the authentication credentials.

Driver conduct is governed through three layered systems that feed into each other: the **shift system** tracks working hours and break compliance; the **rating system** captures passenger-reported service quality; and the **behavioral scoring system** synthesises telemetry data (speeding, harsh braking, phone use) with operational metrics (cancellation rate, acceptance rate, on-time pickups) into a single composite score. Together these systems give fleet managers and compliance officers a 360-degree view of every driver on the network.

=== Driver Operators

Tanzim operates across multiple licensed taxi operators. Each driver belongs to exactly one operator.

[cols="1,2", options="header"]
|===
| Value | Operator
| `NATIONAL_TAXI` | National Taxi Company
| `KABI` | Kabi Ride Services
| `METRO_TAXI` | Metro Taxi
| `DTC` | Dubai Taxi Corporation
| `ARABIA_TAXI` | Arabia Taxi
|===

=== Driver Status Values

[cols="1,3", options="header"]
|===
| Status | Meaning
| `PENDING` | Driver registered but not yet approved to operate
| `ACTIVE` | Approved and able to accept trips when available
| `INACTIVE` | Temporarily not operating (e.g. voluntary leave)
| `SUSPENDED` | Temporarily barred from accepting trips pending investigation
| `BLOCKED` | Blocked from the platform — cannot log in or take rides
| `DEACTIVATED` | Permanently removed from the network
|===

=== Driver Management Endpoints

==== Register a New Driver

`POST /api/v1/drivers`

Registers a new driver on the Tanzim platform. This is a two-step internal operation: first the driver profile is persisted in the Driver Service database, then a corresponding identity account is provisioned in Keycloak using the supplied email and password. Both operations must succeed — if Keycloak provisioning fails after the profile is written, the profile is rolled back and a `500` is returned.

The driver begins in `PENDING` status and cannot go online, accept trips, or be assigned to vehicles until an administrator activates the account. This gate exists to ensure document verification, background checks, and operator onboarding steps are completed before the driver operates on the network.

.Business rules
[cols="1,3", options="header"]
|===
| Rule | Detail
| Uniqueness | The combination of email address, phone number, and licence number must each be unique across the entire platform — not just within an operator. Duplicate values across any of these three fields are rejected with `409`
| Phone format | Phone numbers must be in international format. UAE numbers follow the pattern `+971XXXXXXXXX`. Numbers without a country code are rejected with `400`
| Licence expiry | If `licenseExpiryDate` is supplied and is already in the past, the driver is created in `PENDING` status but will be immediately flagged by the compliance system for licence renewal before activation
| Operator assignment | Every driver must belong to exactly one operator. The `operator` field is immutable after registration — changes require a support workflow
| Password policy | Passwords are passed through to Keycloak and must meet the configured Keycloak password policy (minimum 8 characters, at least one digit and one uppercase letter by default)
|===

.Error scenarios
[cols="1,1,3", options="header"]
|===
| HTTP Status | Condition | Resolution
| 400 | Missing required field | Ensure all required fields are present and non-empty
| 400 | Phone number does not match international format | Reformat to `+[country code][number]`
| 400 | Password does not meet Keycloak policy requirements | Use a password with at least 8 characters including a digit and uppercase letter
| 409 | Email address already registered | Each driver must have a unique email; check for duplicate registrations
| 409 | Phone number already registered | Verify the phone number is not already associated with another account
| 409 | Licence number already registered | A licence can only be registered once on the platform
| 500 | Keycloak account provisioning failed | This is a platform-side issue; retry or contact infrastructure support
|===

==== Get Driver Profile

`GET /api/v1/drivers/{driverId}`

Returns the complete profile for a driver including current status, availability flag, operator, and account timestamps.

==== Get Driver by Employee ID

`GET /api/v1/drivers/employeeId/{employeeId}`

