=== Shift Management Endpoints

A driver shift represents a single bounded work period on the Tanzim network. Shifts enforce regulatory fatigue management rules: each shift runs for a maximum of 12 hours, within which the driver is entitled to a total of 90 minutes of rest breaks, with no individual break exceeding 15 minutes. These limits are enforced server-side — the platform will auto-cap overlong breaks and reject break requests once the allowance is exhausted.

Shifts are the primary unit of record for payroll, regulatory hour submissions, and driver fatigue compliance. Every minute of a shift is classified as either **net driving time** (available for trips) or **break time** (rest). The shift report endpoint exposes both figures for each shift.

The shift system is also coupled to behavioral scoring: a driver who violates break duration limits (recorded as a `BREAK_MAX_TIME_VIOLATED` event) accumulates a penalty against their compliance score. Shifts that end with an open break (driver forgot to end it) have the break automatically closed at shift-end time, and the excess is capped.

==== Shift Business Rules

[cols="1,3", options="header"]
|===
| Rule | Detail
| Shift duration | Fixed at 12 hours. The shift end time is tracked but not auto-enforced — a shift that overruns 12 hours remains open until explicitly ended. Operations managers receive an alert when a shift exceeds its window
| Maximum total break time | 90 minutes per shift. Once this threshold is reached, the `breakAllowanceExhausted` flag is set to `true` and no further breaks can be started for the remainder of the shift
| Maximum single break duration | 15 minutes per break. If the driver ends a break after more than 15 minutes, the platform records the end time as `startTime + 15 minutes`. The actual clock time the driver spent on break does not extend the allowance beyond the cap
| Concurrent breaks | Not permitted. If a driver attempts to start a break while one is already in progress, the request is rejected with `409`
| Concurrent active shifts | A driver can only have one active shift at any time. Starting a shift while one is active returns `409`. Operators must end the previous shift before a new one can begin
| Break during a trip | The platform does not prevent a driver from starting a break while they have an active trip — this is intentional, as the driver may need to pause for a brief stop. However, starting a break while `IN_PROGRESS` on a trip is recorded in the event log for compliance review
| Auto-close on shift end | If the driver ends their shift while a break is still open, the break is automatically closed at the shift-end timestamp before the shift is finalised
|===

==== Start a Driver Shift

`POST /api/v1/shifts/start`

Opens a new 12-hour shift for a driver. The shift start timestamp is recorded at the moment the request is processed. Once started, the driver is eligible to go online and receive trip assignments for the duration of the shift.

[source,json]
----
{ "driverId": 1042 }
----

.Error scenarios
[cols="1,1,3", options="header"]
|===
| HTTP Status | Condition | Resolution
| 400 | `driverId` is missing or invalid | Supply a valid driver ID
| 404 | No driver found for the given ID | Verify the driver exists and is registered
| 409 | Driver already has an active shift | End the existing shift before starting a new one
|===

==== End a Driver Shift

`PATCH /api/v1/shifts/{shiftId}/end`

Closes the shift and finalises all shift metrics. If the driver is on a break at the time this call is made, the open break is automatically closed at the same timestamp before the shift is marked complete. The shift's `netDrivingMinutes` and `totalBreakMinutesUsed` are locked at this point for payroll and reporting.

.Error scenarios
[cols="1,1,3", options="header"]
|===
| HTTP Status | Condition | Resolution
| 404 | Shift ID not found | Verify the shift ID
| 400 | Shift is already closed (not active) | A shift can only be ended once
| 403 | Authenticated driver does not own this shift | Only the driver or an admin can end a shift
|===

==== Start a Break

`POST /api/v1/shifts/{shiftId}/breaks/start`

Begins a rest break within an active shift. The break start time is recorded at the moment of the call. An optional `reason` can be provided for operational records (e.g. "Fuel stop", "Prayer break", "Vehicle check"). Reason values are free-text and not validated against a controlled vocabulary.

[source,json]
----
{ "reason": "Prayer break" }
----

The platform validates that: the shift is currently active; no break is already in progress; and the total break allowance for the shift has not been exhausted.

.Error scenarios
[cols="1,1,3", options="header"]
|===
| HTTP Status | Condition | Resolution
| 400 | Shift is not active | Breaks can only be taken during an active shift
| 409 | A break is already in progress for this shift | End the current break before starting another
| 409 | Break allowance of 90 minutes is fully exhausted | No further breaks are permitted for this shift
| 404 | Shift ID not found | Verify the shift ID
|===

==== End a Break

`PATCH /api/v1/shifts/{shiftId}/breaks/end`

Closes the current open break. The platform computes the break duration. If the break has run for more than 15 minutes, the recorded break end time is silently adjusted back to `breakStart + 15 minutes` — the driver's actual return time is not recorded beyond the cap. This prevents long unauthorised breaks from consuming disproportionate allowance from the 90-minute pool.

.Error scenarios
[cols="1,1,3", options="header"]
|===
| HTTP Status | Condition | Resolution
| 400 | No break is currently in progress for this shift | Cannot end a break that has not started
| 400 | Shift is not active | Cannot manage breaks on a closed shift
| 404 | Shift ID not found | Verify the shift ID
|===

==== Get Shift Details

`GET /api/v1/shifts/{shiftId}`

Returns the full shift state including elapsed time, break usage, remaining allowance, current break status, and a log of all breaks taken.

==== Get Active Shift for Driver

`GET /api/v1/shifts/driver/{driverId}/active`

Returns the driver's currently active shift. Returns 404 if the driver has no active shift.

==== Get All Active Shifts

`GET /api/v1/shifts/active`

Returns all currently active shifts across all drivers. Used by operations supervisors to monitor live fleet shift status.

==== Get Driver Shift History

`GET /api/v1/shifts/driver/{driverId}`

Paginated list of all shifts for a driver, sorted newest first.

==== Get Shifts by Date Range

`GET /api/v1/shifts/driver/{driverId}/range?from={datetime}&to={datetime}`

Returns all shifts for a driver that started within the specified date range. Used for payroll calculation and regulatory reporting.

==== Get Shift Report

`GET /api/v1/shifts/{shiftId}/report`

Returns the full analytics report for a single shift:

[cols="1,3", options="header"]
|===
| Field | Description
| `shiftDurationMinutes` | Total elapsed time from shift start to end (or current time if active)
| `netDrivingMinutes` | Shift duration minus all break time — the actual time available for trips
| `totalBreaksTaken` | Number of breaks recorded in the shift
| `totalBreakMinutesUsed` | Total break time consumed
| `remainingBreakMinutes` | How much break allowance is still available
| `breakAllowanceExhausted` | Whether the 90-minute cap has been hit
| `maxAllowedBreakMinutes` | Always 90 — the platform maximum
| `maxBreakDurationMinutes` | Always 15 — the per-break maximum
| `breaks` | Full list of breaks with individual start, end, duration, and reason
|===

==== Get Shift Reports by Date Range

`GET /api/v1/shifts/driver/{driverId}/report?from={datetime}&to={datetime}`

Returns shift reports for all shifts within the date range. Used for payroll period reporting, regulatory submission, and fatigue compliance audits.

